%U A397967 140637475521356802631791918,6848523053220066390433472825132,727446290803933799930276981833925850,167394854059249960073107069427386488107252
%N A397967 Number of reducible flow graphs on n labeled nodes whose entry node 1 is a global source and node n is a global sink (node 1 = node n when n = 1).
%C A397967 For n >= 2 the source and sink are singleton SCCs. The remaining vertices form an acyclic assembly of reducible single-entry SCC regions: cross-region edges enter region headers, every region is reachable from the source, and every region reaches the sink.
%C A397967 Self-loops multiply by 2^(n-2) for n >= 2 (none on source or sink).
%D A397967 M. S. Hecht and J. D. Ullman, Flow graph reducibility, SIAM J. Comput. 1 (1972), 188-202.
%D A397967 M. S. Hecht and J. D. Ullman, Characterizations of reducible flow graphs, J. ACM 21 (1974), 367-375.
%D A397967 R. W. Robinson, Counting digraphs with restrictions on the strong components, in T.-H. Ku (ed.), Combinatorics and Graph Theory '95, World Scientific, Singapore, 1995, pp. 343-354.
%D A397967 R. E. Tarjan, Testing flow graph reducibility, J. Comput. System Sci. 9 (1974), 355-365.
%F A397967 Put c(m) = m*A397470(m). Let B(0,0) = D(0,0) = 1 and B(v,0) = D(v,0) = 0 for v > 0. For v,k > 0, B(v,k) = Sum_{m=1..v-k+1} binomial(v-1,m-1)*c(m)*B(v-m,k-1), and D(v,k) = Sum_{q=1..k} (-1)^(q+1)*Sum_{w=q..v} binomial(v,w)*B(w,q)*2^(w*(k-q))*D(v-w,k-q). Thus D(v,k) counts acyclic assemblies of k reducible SCC regions on v labeled vertices.
%F A397967 Let A(0,0,r) = 1 and A(v,0,r) = 0 for v > 0. For v,k > 0, A(v,k,r) = 2^(r*k)*D(v,k) - Sum_{j=0..k-1} Sum_{u=0..v} binomial(v,u)*A(u,j,r)*D(v-u,k-j)*2^((v-u)*j). This counts the assemblies in which every region is reachable from a pool of r external vertices.
%F A397967 Define G(0,0) = 1. For v,k > 0, G(v,k) = 2^v*A(v,k,1) - Sum_{u=0..v-1} binomial(v,u)*Sum_{j=0..k} G(u,j)*A(v-u,k-j,1+u), with G(v,0) = 0 for v > 0. Here G(v,k) counts the assemblies in which every one of the v vertices also reaches a separate global sink.
%F A397967 a(1) = a(2) = 1; for n >= 3, a(n) = 2*Sum_{k=1..n-2} G(n-2,k). The factor 2 chooses whether the direct source-to-sink edge is present.
%o A397967 (Python) reducible_labeled_system(14)[5] # See Python link in A398465 for program code.
%Y A397967 Cf. A398465, A350790 (all such digraphs, unpointed).
